  id: Brain_Steam
  partName: Brain Steam
  descriptionChunks:
  - The brain stem is a vital structure connecting the brain to the spinal cord and
    controls essential life functions such as breathing, heart rate, and reflexes.
    It regulates involuntary activities necessary for survival and coordinates signals
    between the brain and body.
  - This region plays a fundamental role in maintaining consciousness and basic physiological
    processes. Any disruption to the brain stem can severely affect vital functions,
    making it one of the most critical components of the nervous system.
